<title>GREECE: Greek capital mkts commission fines shareholders.</title>
<headline>Greek capital mkts commission fines shareholders.</headline>
<dateline>ATHENS 1997-01-28</dateline>
<text>
<p>Greece's capital markets commission fined 12 more large shareholders of Athens stock exchange listings for violating disclosure regulations on changes of ownership stakes, it said on Tuesday.</p>
<p>The capital markets commission fined 24 main shareholders of firms listed on the Athens bourse on January 21.</p>
<p>Having reviewed 25 cases of share transactions which significantly altered ownership stakes in listed companies that were not disclosed to the Athens stock exchange within five days as the presidential decree 51/1992 requires, it fined the following 12 cases:</p>
<p>    NAME		    FINE (drs)	     STOCK</p>
<p> 1. D. Economidis	  16.4 million	     ECON</p>
<p> 2. K. Sarantis	    15.8 million	     SARANTIS</p>
<p> 3. G. Sarantis	    15.8 million	     SARANTIS</p>
<p> 4. S. Sigalas	     14.9 million	     SIGALAS</p>
<p> 5. M. Politis	     13.1 million	     GNOMON</p>
<p> 6. N. Kambas		13.0 million	     GEK</p>
<p> 7. G.Travlos		12.9 million	     TECHNODOMI</p>
<p> 8. D.Travlos		12.9 million	     TECHNODOMI</p>
<p> 9. M.Travlos		12.9 million	     TECHNODOMI</p>
<p> 10.M. Svoli		 12.3 million	     TECHNICAL</p>
<p>OLYMPIAKI  11.P. Sotiriou	     4.6 million	     SHEET STEEL</p>
<p> 12.D. Voilin-Liambei     2.2 million	     ETMA</p>
<p>It said that it went easy on the magnitude of the fines as it was the first time such penalties were applied based on presidential decree 51/1992.</p>
<p>&quot;In deciding the specific fines the commission took into consideration other factors including the nature of share transfers within family members, the value of the transaction and the extent of the change in ownership,&quot; it said. --Dimitris Kontogiannis, Athens Newsroom +301 3311812-4</p>
</text>
